"eCFR :: 47 CFR Part 76 -- Multichannel Video and Cable Television Service (https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76)\nciteturn2180view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76\",\"pattern\":\"Subpart B—\"}); Total lines: 5361\nL436: #### § 76.11 Lockbox enforcement.\nL437: \nL438: Any party aggrieved by the failure or refusal of a cable operator to provided a lockbox as provided for in Title VI of the Communications Act may petition the Commission for relief in accordance with the provisions and procedures set forth in cite101†§ 76.7 for petitions for special relief.\nL439: \nL440: [cite121†50 FR 18661†www.federalregister.gov , May 2, 1985]\nL441: \nL442: ## Subpart B—Registration Statements\nL4558: #### § 76.1506 Carriage of television broadcast signals.\nL4559: \nL4560: (a) The provisions of subpart D shall apply to open video systems in accordance with the provisions contained in this subpart.\nL4561: \nL4562: (b) For the purposes of this subpart S, television stations are significantly viewed when they are viewed in households that do not receive television signals from multichannel video programming distributors as follows:\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\neCFR :: 47 CFR Part 76 -- Multichannel Video and Cable Television Service (https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76)\nciteturn2180view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76\",\"pattern\":\"Subpart C—\"}); Total lines: 5361\nL461: (d) A grant of special temporary authority may be rescinded by the Commission at any time upon a finding of facts which warrant such action.\nL462: \nL463: [cite122†39 FR 35166†www.federalregister.gov , Sept. 30, 1974; cite123†42 FR 19346†www.federalregister.gov , Apr. 13, 1977, as amended at cite124†43 FR 49008†www.federalregister.gov , Oct. 20, 1978]\nL464: ## Subpart C—Cable Franchising\nL465: #### § 76.41 Franchise application process.\nL466: \nL467: (a) Definition. Competitive franchise applicant. For the purpose of this section, an applicant for a cable franchise in an area currently served by another cable operator or cable operators in accordance with cite125†47 U.S.C. 541(a)(1)†www.govinfo.gov .\nL468: \nL469: (b) A competitive franchise applicant must include the following information in writing in its franchise application, in addition to any information required by applicable State and local laws:\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\neCFR :: 47 CFR Part 76 -- Multichannel Video and Cable Television Service (https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76)\nciteturn2180view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76\",\"pattern\":\"Subpart D—\"}); Total lines: 5361\nL156: Any television broadcast station operating on a channel regularly assigned to its community by cite72†§ 73.606 or cite73†§ 73.622 of this chapter , and any television broadcast station licensed by a foreign government: Provided, however, That a television broadcast station licensed by a foreign government shall not be entitled to assert a claim to carriage, program exclusivity, or retransmission consent authorization pursuant to cite70†subpart D or cite71†F of this part , but may otherwise be carried if consistent with the rules on any service tier.\nL157: Further provided that a television broadcast station operating on channels regularly assigned to its community by both cite72†§§ 73.606 and cite73†73.622 of this chapter may assert a claim for carriage pursuant to cite70†subpart D of this part only for a channel assigned pursuant to cite72†§ 73.606 .\nL158: (c) Television translator station. A television broadcast translator station as defined in cite74†§ 74.701 of this chapter .\nL159: \nL160: (d) Grade A and Grade B contours. The field intensity contours defined in cite75†§ 73.683(a) of this chapter .\nL161: (e) Specified zone of a television broadcast station. The area extending 56.3 air km (35 air miles) from the reference point in the community to which that station is licensed or authorized by the Commission. A list of reference points is contained in cite76†§ 76.53 . A television broadcast station that is authorized but not operating has a specified zone that terminates eighteen (18) months after the initial grant of its construction permit.\nL271: (2) In the case of a cable system with more than one headend, the principal headend designated by the cable operator, except that such designation shall not undermine or evade the requirements of cite70†subpart D of this part . Each cable system must provide information regarding the designation and location of the principal headend to the Commission promptly upon request. Except for good cause, an operator may not change its choice of principal headend.\nL508: #### § 76.43 Mixed-use rule.\nL509: \nL510: A franchising authority may not regulate the provision of any services other than cable services offered over the cable system of a cable operator, with the exception of channel capacity on institutional networks.\nL511: \nL512: [cite133†84 FR 44750†www.federalregister.gov , Aug. 27, 2019]\nL513: \nL514: ## Subpart D—Carriage of Television Broadcast Signals\nL1579: (3) With respect to must-carry complaints filed pursuant to cite219†paragraph (b) of this section, such complaints may be filed at any time the complainant believes that the cable television system operator has failed to comply with the applicable provisions of cite70†subpart D of this part .\nL1580: \nL1581: [cite211†58 FR 17362†www.federalregister.gov , Apr. 2, 1993, as amended at cite220†64 FR 6572†www.federalregister.gov , Feb. 10, 1999]\nL4558: #### § 76.1506 Carriage of television broadcast signals.\nL4559: \nL4560: (a) The provisions of subpart D shall apply to open video systems in accordance with the provisions contained in this subpart.\nL4561: \nL4562: (b) For the purposes of this subpart S, television stations are significantly viewed when they are viewed in households that do not receive television signals from multichannel video programming distributors as follows:\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\neCFR :: 47 CFR Part 76 -- Multichannel Video and Cable Television Service (https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76)\nciteturn2180view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76\",\"pattern\":\"Subpart E—\"}); Total lines: 5361\nL1738: (4) Television broadcast station. A television broadcast station is an over-the-air commercial or noncommercial television broadcast station licensed by the Commission under subpart E of cite172†part 73 of title 47, Code of Federal Regulations , except that such term does not include a low-power or translator television station.\nL1917: ## Subpart E—Equal Employment Opportunity Requirements\nL1918: \nL1919: #### Source:\nL1920: \nL1921: cite290†50 FR 40855†www.federalregister.gov , Oct. 7, 1985, unless otherwise noted.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\neCFR :: 47 CFR Part 76 -- Multichannel Video and Cable Television Service (https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76)\nciteturn2180view4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76\",\"pattern\":\"Subpart F—\"}); Total lines: 5361\nL1582: #### § 76.62 Manner of carriage.\nL1583: \nL1584: (a) Cable operators shall carry the entirety of the program schedule of any television station (including low power television stations) carried by the system unless carriage of specific programming is prohibited, and other programming authorized to be substituted, under cite221†§ 76.67 or subpart F of part 76, or unless carriage is pursuant to a valid retransmission consent agreement for the entire signal or any portion thereof as provided in cite189†§ 76.64 .\nL2037: ## Subpart F—Network Non-duplication Protection, Syndicated Exclusivity and Sports Blackout\nL2038: \nL2039: #### Source:\nL2040: \nL2041: cite305†65 FR 68101†www.federalregister.gov , Nov. 14, 2000, unless otherwise noted.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\neCFR :: 47 CFR Part 76 -- Multichannel Video and Cable Television Service (https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76)\nciteturn2180view5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76\",\"pattern\":\"Subpart G—\"}); Total lines: 5361\nL297: (b) Copies to be filed. Unless otherwise directed by specific regulation or the Commission, an original and two (2) copies of all pleadings shall be filed in accordance with cite94†§ 0.401(a) of this chapter , except that petitions requiring fees as set forth at cite95†part 1, subpart G of this chapter must be filed in accordance with cite96†§ 0.401(b) of this chapter .\nL2274: [cite305†65 FR 68101†www.federalregister.gov , Nov. 14, 2000, as amended at cite317†79 FR 63562†www.federalregister.gov , Oct. 24, 2014]\nL2275: ## Subpart G—Cablecasting\nL2276: #### § 76.205 Origination cablecasts by legally qualified candidates for public office; equal opportunities.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\neCFR :: 47 CFR Part 76 -- Multichannel Video and Cable Television Service (https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76)\nciteturn2180view6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76\",\"pattern\":\"Subpart H—\"}); Total lines: 5361\nL2388: #### § 76.227 [Reserved]\nL2389: \nL2390: ## Subpart H—General Operating Requirements\nL2391: #### § 76.309 Customer service obligations.\nL2392: \nL2393: (a) A cable franchise authority may enforce the customer service standards set forth in cite358†paragraph (c) of this section against cable operators. The franchise authority must provide affected cable operators ninety (90) days written notice of its intent to enforce the standards.\nL2394: \nL2395: (b) Nothing in this rule should be construed to prevent or prohibit:\nL4111: (3) A cable operator, or a satellite cable programming vendor or a satellite broadcast programming vendor has denied or failed to acknowledge a request to purchase or negotiate to purchase satellite cable programming, satellite broadcast programming, or terrestrial cable programming, or a request to amend an existing contract pertaining to such programming pursuant to cite682†§ 76.1002(f) , allegedly in violation of one or more of the rules contained in this subpart.\nL4112: \nL4113: (h) Remedies for violations —\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\neCFR :: 47 CFR Part 76 -- Multichannel Video and Cable Television Service (https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76)\nciteturn2180view7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76\",\"pattern\":\"Subpart I—\"}); Total lines: 5361\nL2450: (c) Compliance with this section is required by December 19, 2024, except that for cable operators with annual receipts of $47 million or less, compliance is not required until March 19, 2025.\nL2451: \nL2452: [cite366†89 FR 28679†www.federalregister.gov , Apr. 19, 2024, as amended at cite367†89 FR 87984†www.federalregister.gov , Nov. 6, 2024]\nL2453: ## Subpart I [Reserved]\nL2454: \nL2455: ## Subpart J—Ownership of Cable Systems\nL2456: #### § 76.501 Cross-ownership.\nL2457: \nL2458: (a)-(c) [Reserved]\nL2459: \nL2460: (d) No cable operator shall offer satellite master antenna television service (“SMATV”), as that service is defined in cite368†§ 76.5(a)(2) , separate and apart from any franchised cable service in any portion of the franchise area served by that cable operator's cable system, either directly or indirectly through an affiliate owned, operated, controlled, or under common control with the cable operator.\nL2461: \nL2462: (e)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\neCFR :: 47 CFR Part 76 -- Multichannel Video and Cable Television Service (https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76)\nciteturn2180view8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76\",\"pattern\":\"Subpart J—\"}); Total lines: 5361\nL2450: (c) Compliance with this section is required by December 19, 2024, except that for cable operators with annual receipts of $47 million or less, compliance is not required until March 19, 2025.\nL2453: ## Subpart I [Reserved]\nL2454: \nL2455: ## Subpart J—Ownership of Cable Systems\nL2456: #### § 76.501 Cross-ownership.\nL2457: \nL2458: (a)-(c) [Reserved]\nL2459: \nL2460: (d) No cable operator shall offer satellite master antenna television service (“SMATV”), as that service is defined in cite368†§ 76.5(a)(2) , separate and apart from any franchised cable service in any portion of the franchise area served by that cable operator's cable system, either directly or indirectly through an affiliate owned, operated, controlled, or under common control with the cable operator.\nL2461: \nL2462: (e)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\neCFR :: 47 CFR Part 76 -- Multichannel Video and Cable Television Service (https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76)\nciteturn2180view9 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76\",\"pattern\":\"Subpart K—\"}); Total lines: 5361\nL266: (oo) Usable activated channels. Those activated channels of a cable system, except those channels whose use for the distribution of broadcast signals would conflict with technical and safety regulations. See part 76, subpart K.\nL267: \nL268: (pp) Principal headend.\nL269: \nL270: (1) The headend, in the case of a cable system with a single headend or,\nL1585: (b) Each digital television broadcast signal carried shall be carried without material degradation. Each analog television broadcast signal carried shall be carried without material degradation and in compliance with technical standards set forth in cite222†subpart K of this part .\nL2630: ## Subpart K—Technical Standards\nL3073: (h) If an alternative video programming service provider connects its wiring to the home wiring before the incumbent cable operator has terminated service and has capped off its line to prevent signal leakage, the alternative video programming service provider shall be responsible for ensuring that the incumbent's wiring is properly capped off in accordance with the Commission's signal leakage requirements.\nL3074: See subpart K (technical standards) of the Commission's Cable Television Service rules (cite502†47 CFR 76.605(a)(13) and cite503†76.610 through cite466†76.617 ).\nL3075: (i) Where the subscriber terminates cable service but will not be using the home wiring to receive another alternative video programming service, the cable operator shall properly cap off its own line in accordance with the Commission's signal leakage requirements. See subpart K (technical standards) of the Commission's Cable Television Service rules (cite502†47 CFR 76.605(a)(13) and cite503†76.610 through cite466†76.617 ).\nL3076: (j) Cable operators are prohibited from using any ownership interests they may have in property located on the subscriber's side of the demarcation point, such as molding or conduit, to prevent, impede, or in any way interfere with, a subscriber's right to use his or her home wiring to receive an alternative service. In addition, incumbent cable operators must take reasonable steps within their control to ensure that an alternative service provider has access to the home wiring at the demarcation point.\nL5029: #### § 76.1717 Compliance with technical standards.\nL5030: \nL5031: Each system operator shall be prepared to show, on request by an authorized representative of the Commission or the local franchising authority, that the system does, in fact, comply with the technical standards rules in part 76, subpart K.\nL5032: \nL5033: ## Subpart V—Reports and Filings\nL5034: \nL5035: #### Source:\nL5036: \nL5037: cite855†65 FR 53623†www.federalregister.gov , Sept. 5, 2000, unless otherwise noted.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\neCFR :: 47 CFR Part 76 -- Multichannel Video and Cable Television Service (https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76)\nciteturn2180view10 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76\",\"pattern\":\"Subpart L—\"}); Total lines: 5361\nL3017: [cite496†68 FR 66734†www.federalregister.gov , Nov. 28, 2003, as amended at cite497†76 FR 40279†www.federalregister.gov , July 8, 2011; cite475†83 FR 7630†www.federalregister.gov , Feb. 22, 2018]\nL3018: ## Subpart L—Cable Television Access\nL3019: #### § 76.701 Leased access channels.\nL3020: (a) Notwithstanding cite46†47 U.S.C. 532(b)(2)†www.govinfo.gov (Communications Act of 1934, as amended, section 612), a cable operator, in accordance with 【46†47 U.S.C.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\neCFR :: 47 CFR Part 76 -- Multichannel Video and Cable Television Service (https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76)\nciteturn2180view11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76\",\"pattern\":\"Subpart N—\"}); Total lines: 5361\nL3151: ## Subpart N—Cable Rate Regulation\nL3152: \nL3153: #### Source:\nL3154: \nL3155: cite519†58 FR 29753†www.federalregister.gov , May 21, 1993, unless otherwise noted.\nL3156: \nL3157: ###### Effective Date Note\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\neCFR :: 47 CFR Part 76 -- Multichannel Video and Cable Television Service (https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76)\nciteturn2180view12 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76\",\"pattern\":\"Subpart O—\"}); Total lines: 5361\nL3926: ## Subpart O—Competitive Access to Cable Programming\nL3944: Such entities include, but are not limited to, a cable operator, a BRS/EBS provider, a direct broadcast satellite service, a television receive-only satellite program distributor, and a satellite master antenna television system operator, as well as buying groups or agents of all such entities.\nL3945: Note to paragraph (e):\nL3946: \nL3947: A video programming provider that provides more than one channel of video programming on an open video system is a multichannel video programming distributor for purposes of this subpart O and cite651†Section 76.1507 .\nL3948: (f) Satellite broadcast programming. The term “satellite broadcast programming” means broadcast video programming when such programming is retransmitted by satellite and the entity retransmitting such programming is not the broadcaster or an entity performing such retransmission on behalf of and with the specific consent of the broadcaster.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\neCFR :: 47 CFR Part 76 -- Multichannel Video and Cable Television Service (https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76)\nciteturn2180view13 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76\",\"pattern\":\"Subpart P—\"}); Total lines: 5361\nL4165: #### §§ 76.1005-76.1010 [Reserved]\nL4166: \nL4167: ## Subpart P—Competitive Availability of Navigation Devices\nL4168: \nL4169: #### Source:\nL4170: \nL4171: cite694†63 FR 38094†www.federalregister.gov , July 15, 1998, unless otherwise noted.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\neCFR :: 47 CFR Part 76 -- Multichannel Video and Cable Television Service (https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76)\nciteturn2180view14 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76\",\"pattern\":\"Subpart Q—\"}); Total lines: 5361\nL4234: #### § 76.1210 Effect on other rules.\nL4235: \nL4236: Nothing in this subpart affects cite703†§ 64.702(d) of the Commission's regulations or other Commission regulations governing interconnection and competitive provision of customer premises equipment used in connection with basic common carrier communications services.\nL4237: \nL4238: ## Subpart Q—Regulation of Carriage Agreements\nL4239: \nL4240: #### Source:\nL4241: \nL4242: cite704†58 FR 60395†www.federalregister.gov , Nov. 16, 1993, unless otherwise noted.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\neCFR :: 47 CFR Part 76 -- Multichannel Video and Cable Television Service (https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76)\nciteturn2180view15 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76\",\"pattern\":\"Subpart R—\"}); Total lines: 5361\nL4339: #### §§ 76.1303-76.1305 [Reserved]\nL4340: \nL4341: ## Subpart R—Telecommunications Act Implementation\nL4342: \nL4343: #### Source:\nL4344: \nL4345: cite693†61 FR 18980†www.federalregister.gov , Apr. 30, 1996, unless otherwise noted.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\neCFR :: 47 CFR Part 76 -- Multichannel Video and Cable Television Service (https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76)\nciteturn2180view16 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76\",\"pattern\":\"Subpart S—\"}); Total lines: 5361\nL4355: ## Subpart S—Open Video Systems\nL4356: \nL4357: #### Source:\nL4358: \nL4359: cite656†61 FR 28708†www.federalregister.gov , June 5, 1996, unless otherwise noted.\nL4360: #### § 76.1500 Definitions.\nL4361: \nL4362: (a) Open video system. A facility consisting of a set of transmission paths and associated signal generation, reception, and control equipment that is designed to provide cable service which includes video programming and which is provided to multiple subscribers within a community, provided that the Commission has certified that such system complies with this part.\nL4558: #### § 76.1506 Carriage of television broadcast signals.\nL4559: \nL4560: (a) The provisions of subpart D shall apply to open video systems in accordance with the provisions contained in this subpart.\nL4561: \nL4562: (b) For the purposes of this subpart S, television stations are significantly viewed when they are viewed in households that do not receive television signals from multichannel video programming distributors as follows:\nL4628: The following sections within part 76 shall also apply to open video systems: cite772†§§ 76.71 , cite773†76.73 , cite301†76.75 , cite774†76.77 , cite775†76.79 , cite302†76.1702 , and cite776†76.1802 (Equal Employment Opportunity Requirements); cite387†§§ 76.503 and cite777†76.504 (ownership restrictions); cite778†§ 76.981 (negative option billing); and cite779†§§ 76.1300 , cite708†76.1301 and cite780†76.1302 (regulation of carriage agreements); cite503†§ 76.610 (operation in the frequency bands 108-137 and 225-400 MHz—scope of application provided, however, that these sections shall apply to open video systems only to the extent that they do not conflict with this subpart S.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\neCFR :: 47 CFR Part 76 -- Multichannel Video and Cable Television Service (https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76)\nciteturn2180view17 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76\",\"pattern\":\"Subpart T—\"}); Total lines: 5361\nL4702: ## Subpart T—Notices\nL4703: \nL4704: #### Source:\nL4705: \nL4706: cite637†65 FR 53617†www.federalregister.gov , Sept. 5, 2000, unless otherwise noted.\nL4707: #### § 76.1600 Electronic delivery of notices.\nL4708: (a) Except as provided in cite360†§ 76.1603 for changes that occur due to circumstances outside a cable operator's control, which also may be provided as set forth in 76.1603(b), written information provided by cable operators to subscribers or customers pursuant to cite787†§§ 76.1601 , cite788†76.1602 , cite789†76.1603 , cite790†76.1604 , cite791†76.1618 , and cite792†76.1620 of this subpart T, as well as subscriber privacy notifications required by cable operators, satellite providers, and open video systems pursuant to sections 631, 338(i), and 653 of the Communications Act, may be delivered electronically by email to any subscriber who has not opted out of electronic delivery under cite793†paragraph (a)(3) of this section if the entity:\nL4709: (1) Sends the notice to the subscriber's or customer's verified email address;\nL4710: \nL4711: (2) Provides either the entirety of the written information or a weblink to the written information in the notice; and\nL4712: \nL4713: (3) Includes, in the body of the notice, a telephone number that is clearly and prominently presented to subscribers so that it is readily identifiable as an opt-out mechanism that will allow subscribers to continue to receive paper copies of the written material.\nL4714: (b) For purposes of this section, a verified email address is defined as:\nL4715: \nL4716: (1) An email address that the subscriber has provided to the cable operator (and not vice versa) for purposes of receiving communication;\nL4717: \nL4718: (2) An email address that the subscriber regularly uses to communicate with the cable operator; or\nL4719: \nL4720: (3) An email address that has been confirmed by the subscriber as an appropriate vehicle for the delivery of notices.\nL4721: (c) Cable operators that provide written Subpart T notices via paper copy may provide certain portions of the cite794†§ 76.1602 annual notices electronically, to any subscriber who has not opted out of electronic delivery under cite793†paragraphs (a)(3) or cite795†(c)(3) of this section, by prominently displaying the following on the front or first page of the printed annual notice:\nL4722: (1) A weblink in a form that is short, simple, and easy to remember, leading to written information required to be provided pursuant to cite796†§ 76.1602(b)(2) , cite797†(7) , and cite798†(8) ;\nL4723: \nL4724: (2) A weblink in a form that is short, simple, and easy to remember, leading to written information required to be provided pursuant to cite799†§ 76.1602(b)(5) ; and\nL4896: (8) Sponsorship identification. Whenever sponsorship announcements are omitted pursuant to cite829†§ 76.1615(f) of Subpart T, the cable television system operator shall maintain a list in accordance with cite830†§ 76.1715 ;\nL5019: #### § 76.1715 Sponsorship identification.\nL5020: \nL5021: Whenever sponsorship announcements are omitted pursuant to cite829†§ 76.1615(f) of subpart T, the cable television system operator shall observe the following conditions:\nL5022: \nL5023: (a) Maintain a list showing the name, address, and (where available) the telephone number of each advertiser;\nL5024: \nL5025: (b) Make this list available to members of the public who have a legitimate interest in obtaining the information contained in the list.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\neCFR :: 47 CFR Part 76 -- Multichannel Video and Cable Television Service (https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76)\nciteturn2180view18 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76\",\"pattern\":\"Subpart U—\"}); Total lines: 5361\nL4874: #### §§ 76.1621-76.1622 [Reserved]\nL4875: \nL4876: ## Subpart U—Documents to be Maintained for Inspection\nL4877: \nL4878: #### Source:\nL4879: \nL4880: cite823†65 FR 53621†www.federalregister.gov , Sept. 5, 2000, unless otherwise noted.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\neCFR :: 47 CFR Part 76 -- Multichannel Video and Cable Television Service (https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76)\nciteturn2180view19 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76\",\"pattern\":\"Subpart V—\"}); Total lines: 5361\nL5029: #### § 76.1717 Compliance with technical standards.\nL5030: \nL5031: Each system operator shall be prepared to show, on request by an authorized representative of the Commission or the local franchising authority, that the system does, in fact, comply with the technical standards rules in part 76, subpart K.\nL5032: \nL5033: ## Subpart V—Reports and Filings\nL5034: \nL5035: #### Source:\nL5036: \nL5037: cite855†65 FR 53623†www.federalregister.gov , Sept. 5, 2000, unless otherwise noted.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\neCFR :: 47 CFR Part 76 -- Multichannel Video and Cable Television Service (https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76)\nciteturn2180view20 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: find({\"ref_id\":\"https://www.ecfr.gov/current/title-47/chapter-I/subchapter-C/part-76\",\"pattern\":\"Subpart W—\"}); Total lines: 5361\nL5099: ## Subpart W—Encoding Rules\nL5100: \nL5101: #### Source:\nL5102: \nL5103: cite861†68 FR 66735†www.federalregister.gov , Nov. 28, 2003, unless otherwise noted.\nL5104: #### § 76.1909 Redistribution control of unencrypted digital terrestrial broadcast content.\nL5105: \nL5106: (a) For the purposes of this section, the terms unencrypted digital terrestrial broadcast content, EIT, PMT, broadcast flag, covered demodulator product, and marked content shall have the same meaning as set forth in cite862†§ 73.9000 of this chapter .\n"
